I'll find and fix the bug in the `off` implementation.Found the bug. At `src/index.ts:86`, when the handler isn't found, `handlers.indexOf(handler)` returns `-1`, and `splice(-1, 1)` removes the **last** handler instead of doing nothing.

Fix: only splice when `indexOf` returns a valid index. I'll also add a regression test.Fixed in `src/index.ts` and added a regression test in `test/index_test.ts`.

**Cause:** `off(type, handler)` called `handlers.splice(handlers.indexOf(handler), 1)`. When the handler was not registered, `indexOf` returned `-1`, and `splice(-1, 1)` removes the **last** element of the array (`src/index.ts:86`).

**Fix:** only splice when `indexOf` finds the handler:

```ts
const index = handlers.indexOf(handler);
if (index !== -1) handlers.splice(index, 1);
```

